{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nimport bisect\n\nn1 = n // 2\nleft_sums = []\nright_sums = []\n\ndef compute_sums(arr, start, end, result_list):\n    stack = [(start, 0)]\n    while stack:\n        idx, s = stack.pop()\n        if idx == end:\n            result_list.append(s % m)\n        else:\n            stack.append((idx + 1, (s + arr[idx]) % m))\n            stack.append((idx + 1, s))\n\ncompute_sums(a, 0, n1, left_sums)\ncompute_sums(a, n1, n, right_sums)\n\nans = 0\nleft_sums = sorted(set(left_sums))\n\nfor r_val in right_sums:\n    complement = m - r_val\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(left_sums, complement)\n    if idx > 0:\n        candidate = (left_sums[idx - 1] + r_val) % m\n        ans = max(ans, candidate)\n    if idx < len(left_sums):\n        candidate = (left_sums[idx] + r_val) % m\n        ans = max(ans, candidate)\n\nprint(ans)\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int m = sc.nextInt();\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            a[i] = sc.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        int n1 = n / 2;\n        List<Integer> leftSums = new ArrayList<>();\n        List<Integer> rightSums = new ArrayList<>();\n\n        computeSums(a, 0, n1, m, leftSums);\n        computeSums(a, n1, n, m, rightSums);\n\n        int ans = 0;\n        Set<Integer> leftSet = new HashSet<>(leftSums);\n        List<Integer> leftList = new ArrayList<>(leftSet);\n        Collections.sort(leftList);\n\n        for (int rVal : rightSums) {\n            int complement = (m - rVal) % m;\n            int idx = Collections.binarySearch(leftList, complement);\n            if (idx < 0) {\n                idx = -idx - 1;\n            }\n\n            if (idx > 0) {\n                int candidate = (leftList.get(idx - 1) + rVal) % m;\n                ans = Math.max(ans, candidate);\n            }\n            if (idx < leftList.size()) {\n                int candidate = (leftList.get(idx) + rVal) % m;\n                ans = Math.max(ans, candidate);\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n\n    private static void computeSums(int[] arr, int start, int end, int m, List<Integer> resultList) {\n        Deque<int[]> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        stack.push(new int[]{start, 0});\n\n        while (!stack.isEmpty()) {\n            int[] current = stack.pop();\n            int idx = current[0];\n            int s = current[1];\n\n            if (idx == end) {\n                resultList.add(s % m);\n            } else {\n                stack.push(new int[]{idx + 1, (s + arr[idx]) % m});\n                stack.push(new int[]{idx + 1, s});\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "tok